  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two charged particles, having same kinetic energy, are allowed to pass through a uniform magnetic field perpendicular to the direction of motion. If the ratio of radii of their circular paths is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and their respective masses ratio is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Then, the ratio of their charges will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
